{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "letter-to-noah-c-saxton-4-january-1833", "page": "5", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-noah-c-saxton-4-january-1833/1"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-noah-c-saxton-4-january-1833/2"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-noah-c-saxton-4-january-1833/3"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-noah-c-saxton-4-january-1833/4"}, {"image": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_018_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "18", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-noah-c-saxton-4-january-1833/5"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-noah-c-saxton-4-january-1833", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD2", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to Noah C. Saxton, 4 January 1833", "editorialPageNumber": "18", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/2478323/2478323-0005.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> a scene of <span class=\"underscore\">bloodshed</span> as has not a parallel in the hystory of our nation pestalence hail famine and earthquake will sweep the wicked of this generation from off the face of this Land<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12043950338804792405\"><a href=\"#12043950338804792405\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans38\"><span id=\"documenttrans38\">38</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This information was included in a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 25\nDecember 1832 [D&amp;C 87]\">revelation</a> dictated less than two weeks earlier. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 25\nDecember 1832 [D&amp;C 87]\">Revelation, 25 Dec. 1832</a> [D&amp;C 87].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> to open and prepare the way for the return of the lost tribes of Israel from the north country—<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4053250117868836041\"><a href=\"#4053250117868836041\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans39\"><span id=\"documenttrans39\">39</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Jeremiah 23:8; 31:7–8; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-3-november-1831-dc-133\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-3-november-1831-dc-133\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 3 November 1831 [D&amp;C\n 133]\">Revelation, 3 Nov. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 133:26].</p><hr></div></div></aside> The people of the Lord, those who have complied with the requsitions of the new covenant have already commenced gathering together to <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5646412142282349559\"><a href=\"#5646412142282349559\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4116\" topic=\"x4116\" title=\"Zion\">Zion</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Zion\"><p>A specific location in Missouri; also a literal or figurative gathering of believers in Jesus Christ, characterized by adherence to ideals of harmony, equality, and purity. In JS’s earliest revelations “the cause of Zion” was used to broadly describe the ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/zion\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> which is in the State of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"19145179139107055\"><a href=\"#19145179139107055\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc140\" place=\"plc140\" title=\"Missouri\">Missouri</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Missouri\"><p>Area acquired by U.S. in Louisiana Purchase, 1803, and established as territory, 1812. Missouri Compromise, 1820, admitted Missouri as slave state, 1821. Population in 1830 about 140,000; in 1836 about 240,000; and in 1840 about 380,000. Latter-day Saint ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/missouri\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13492476177871465288\"><a href=\"#13492476177871465288\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans40\"><span id=\"documenttrans40\">40</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">A July 1831 <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 20 July 1831 [D&amp;C\n57]\">revelation</a> designated “the land of <a href=\"/place/missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Missorie</a>” as the place the Lord had “appointed &amp; <a href=\"/topic/consecration\" class=\"referenceInPop\">consecrated</a> for the <a href=\"/topic/gathering\" class=\"referenceInPop\">gethering</a> of the Saints.” <span class=\"title\">The Evening and the Morning Star</span> reported in November 1832 that “since the gathering commenced, which is a little over a year, the number of the disciples which have come from the east, and which have been <a href=\"/topic/baptism\" class=\"referenceInPop\">baptized</a> in this region, is 465[.] Children and those not members, about 345[.] Total 810.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 20 July 1831 [D&amp;C\n57]\">Revelation, 20 July 1831</a> [D&amp;C 57:1]; “The Gathering,” <span class=\"title\">The Evening and the Morning Star,</span> Nov. 1832, [5].)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"> <span class=\"title\">The Evening and the Morning Star.</span> Independence, MO, June 1832–July 1833; Kirtland, OH, Dec. 1833–Sept. 1834.</p></div></div></div></aside> Therefore I declare unto you the warning which the lord has commanded me to declare unto this generation, rembring [remembering] that the eyes of my maker are upon me and that to him I am accountabl for evry word I say wishing nothing worse to my fellow men then their eternal salvation therefore fear God, and give glory to him for the hour of his Judgment is come,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13449693552515773374\"><a href=\"#13449693552515773374\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans41\"><span id=\"documenttrans41\">41</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Revelation 14:7.</p><hr></div></div></aside> Repent ye Repent, ye and imbrace the everlasting Covenant and flee to Zion before the overflowing scourge overtake you, For there are those now living upon the earth whose eyes shall not be closed in death until they see all these things which I have spoken fulfilled<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6601034410058839193\"><a href=\"#6601034410058839193\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans42\"><span id=\"documenttrans42\">42</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" poptitle=\"Revelation, circa 7 March 1831 [D&amp;C\n45]\">Revelation, ca. 7 Mar. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 45:31].</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"underscore\">Remember</span> these things, call upon the Lord while he is near and seek him while he may be found<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9407007647424173813\"><a href=\"#9407007647424173813\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans43\"><span id=\"documenttrans43\">43</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 55:6; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-27-28-december-1832-dc-881-126\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-27-28-december-1832-dc-881-126\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 27–28 December 1832 [D&amp;C 88:1–126]\">Revelation, 27–28 Dec. 1832</a> [D&amp;C 88:62–63].</p><hr></div></div></aside> is the exhortation of your unworthy servant</div><div class=\"right wasptag\">Joseph Smith J<span class=\"underscore\">r</span></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">To <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10843661668912217136\"><a href=\"#10843661668912217136\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per511\" person=\"per511\" title=\"Noah Chapin Saxton\">N. E. Sextan [Noah C. Saxton]</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Saxton, Noah Chapin\"><p>25 Jan. 1798–23 June 1834. Evangelist, Christian newspaper editor. Born in Wilbraham, Hampden Co., Massachusetts. Son of Noah Saxton and Patty Bliss. Graduated from Union College in Schenectady, Schenectady Co., New York, 1818. Received preacher license, ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/noah-chapin-saxton\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside> <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11026829055422473753\"><a href=\"#11026829055422473753\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc70\" place=\"plc70\" title=\"Rochester, New York\">Rochester</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Rochester, New York\"><p>Located at falls of Genesee River, seven miles south of Lake Ontario, on Erie Canal. Founded 1812. Incorporated as village, 1817. Originally called Rochesterville; name changed to Rochester, 1822. Incorporated as city, 1834. County seat. Population in 1820...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/rochester-new-york\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> N Y.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7524937953592665170\"><a href=\"#7524937953592665170\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans1\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in handwriting of <a href=\"/person/william-wines-phelps\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William W. Phelps</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside> [p. 18]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> a scene of <span class=\"underscore\">bloodshed</span> as has not a parallel in the hystory <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of our nation pestalence hail famine and earthquake will <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>sweep the wicked of<span class=\"deleted\">f</span> this generation from off the face of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>this Land<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13369129436569570665\"><a href=\"#13369129436569570665\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans38\"><span id=\"documenttrans38\">38</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This information was included in a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 25\nDecember 1832 [D&amp;C 87]\">revelation</a> dictated less than two weeks earlier. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 25\nDecember 1832 [D&amp;C 87]\">Revelation, 25 Dec. 1832</a> [D&amp;C 87].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> to open and prepare the way for the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>return of the lost tribes of Israel from the north <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>country—<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"469230990012242346\"><a href=\"#469230990012242346\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans39\"><span id=\"documenttrans39\">39</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Jeremiah 23:8; 31:7–8; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-3-november-1831-dc-133\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-3-november-1831-dc-133\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 3 November 1831 [D&amp;C\n 133]\">Revelation, 3 Nov. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 133:26].</p><hr></div></div></aside> The people of the Lord, those who have <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>complied with the requsitions of the new covenant <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>have already commenced gathering togethe[r] to <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16377483789673451455\"><a href=\"#16377483789673451455\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4116\" topic=\"x4116\" title=\"Zion\">Zion</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Zion\"><p>A specific location in Missouri; also a literal or figurative gathering of believers in Jesus Christ, characterized by adherence to ideals of harmony, equality, and purity. In JS’s earliest revelations “the cause of Zion” was used to broadly describe the ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/zion\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>which is in the State of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6809787512230280183\"><a href=\"#6809787512230280183\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc140\" place=\"plc140\" title=\"Missouri\">Missouri</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Missouri\"><p>Area acquired by U.S. in Louisiana Purchase, 1803, and established as territory, 1812. Missouri Compromise, 1820, admitted Missouri as slave state, 1821. Population in 1830 about 140,000; in 1836 about 240,000; and in 1840 about 380,000. Latter-day Saint ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/missouri\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11442147168968945572\"><a href=\"#11442147168968945572\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans40\"><span id=\"documenttrans40\">40</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">A July 1831 <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 20 July 1831 [D&amp;C\n57]\">revelation</a> designated “the land of <a href=\"/place/missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Missorie</a>” as the place the Lord had “appointed &amp; <a href=\"/topic/consecration\" class=\"referenceInPop\">consecrated</a> for the <a href=\"/topic/gathering\" class=\"referenceInPop\">gethering</a> of the Saints.” <span class=\"title\">The Evening and the Morning Star</span> reported in November 1832 that “since the gathering commenced, which is a little over a year, the number of the disciples which have come from the east, and which have been <a href=\"/topic/baptism\" class=\"referenceInPop\">baptized</a> in this region, is 465[.] Children and those not members, about 345[.] Total 810.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 20 July 1831 [D&amp;C\n57]\">Revelation, 20 July 1831</a> [D&amp;C 57:1]; “The Gathering,” <span class=\"title\">The Evening and the Morning Star,</span> Nov. 1832, [5].)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"> <span class=\"title\">The Evening and the Morning Star.</span> Independence, MO, June 1832–July 1833; Kirtland, OH, Dec. 1833–Sept. 1834.</p></div></div></div></aside> Therefore I decl<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>are unto you the warning which the lord <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>has commanded me to declare unto this <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>generation, rembring [remembering] that the eyes of my maker <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>are upon me and that to him I am accountabl <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>for evry word I say wishing nothing worse to <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>my fellow men then their eternal salvation <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>therefore fear God, and give glory to him for <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the hour of his Judgment is come,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9896968557164312818\"><a href=\"#9896968557164312818\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans41\"><span id=\"documenttrans41\">41</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Revelation 14:7.</p><hr></div></div></aside> &lt;​Repent <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ye​&gt; Repent, ye and imbrace the everlasting <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Covenant and flee to Zion before the over<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>flowing scourge overtake you, For there are <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>those now living upon the earth whose eyes <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>shall not be closed in death until they see <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>all these things which I have spoken fulfilled<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18004966126904590530\"><a href=\"#18004966126904590530\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans42\"><span id=\"documenttrans42\">42</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" poptitle=\"Revelation, circa 7 March 1831 [D&amp;C\n45]\">Revelation, ca. 7 Mar. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 45:31].</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"underscore\">Rem[em]ber</span> these things, call upon the Lord <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>while he is near and seek him while <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>he may be found<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13163452300089257383\"><a href=\"#13163452300089257383\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans43\"><span id=\"documenttrans43\">43</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 55:6; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-27-28-december-1832-dc-881-126\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-27-28-december-1832-dc-881-126\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 27–28 December 1832 [D&amp;C 88:1–126]\">Revelation, 27–28 Dec. 1832</a> [D&amp;C 88:62–63].</p><hr></div></div></aside> is the exhortation of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>your unworthy servant</div><div class=\"right wasptag\">Joseph Smith J<span class=\"underscore\">r</span></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">&lt;​To <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9583558685435820850\"><a href=\"#9583558685435820850\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per511\" person=\"per511\" title=\"Noah Chapin Saxton\">N. E. Sextan [Noah C. Saxton]</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Saxton, Noah Chapin\"><p>25 Jan. 1798–23 June 1834. Evangelist, Christian newspaper editor. Born in Wilbraham, Hampden Co., Massachusetts. Son of Noah Saxton and Patty Bliss. Graduated from Union College in Schenectady, Schenectady Co., New York, 1818. Received preacher license, ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/noah-chapin-saxton\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside> <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9958849898932315462\"><a href=\"#9958849898932315462\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc70\" place=\"plc70\" title=\"Rochester, New York\">Rochester</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Rochester, New York\"><p>Located at falls of Genesee River, seven miles south of Lake Ontario, on Erie Canal. Founded 1812. Incorporated as village, 1817. Originally called Rochesterville; name changed to Rochester, 1822. Incorporated as city, 1834. County seat. Population in 1820...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/rochester-new-york\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> N Y.​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15853751616688612629\"><a href=\"#15853751616688612629\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans1\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in handwriting of <a href=\"/person/william-wines-phelps\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William W. Phelps</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside> [p. 18]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Letter to Noah C. Saxton, 4 January 1833", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-noah-c-saxton-4-january-1833/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Letterbook 1", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letterbook-1/26", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Letter to Noah C. Saxton, 4 January 1833, as Published in <em xmlns:tei=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\">American Revivalist, and Rochester Observer</em>", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-noah-c-saxton-4-january-1833-as-published-in-american-revivalist-and-rochester-observer/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "History, 1838–1856, volume A-1 [23 December 1805–30 August 1834]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-a-1-23-december-1805-30-august-1834/263", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "“History of Joseph Smith”", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-of-joseph-smith/154", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_018_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_018_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_018.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_018_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/7633/7633_ms155_2_01_lb1_018.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "139", "requestedPageNumber": "5", "numberOfPages": "5", "editorialTitle": "Letter to Noah C. Saxton, 4 January 1833", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Letter to Noah C. Saxton, 4 January 1833", "date": "January 4, 1833", "handwriting": "Handwriting of Frederick G. Williams", "footnotes": [{"id": "13369129436569570665", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">This information was included in a <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 25\nDecember 1832 [D&amp;C 87]\">revelation</a> dictated less than two weeks earlier. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-25-december-1832-dc-87\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 25\nDecember 1832 [D&amp;C 87]\">Revelation, 25 Dec. 1832</a> [D&amp;C 87].)</p></body></html>", "number": 38, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "469230990012242346", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Jeremiah 23:8; 31:7–8; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-3-november-1831-dc-133\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-3-november-1831-dc-133\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 3 November 1831 [D&amp;C\n 133]\">Revelation, 3 Nov. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 133:26].</p></body></html>", "number": 39, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "11442147168968945572", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">A July 1831 <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 20 July 1831 [D&amp;C\n57]\">revelation</a> designated “the land of <a href=\"/place/missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Missorie</a>” as the place the Lord had “appointed &amp; <a href=\"/topic/consecration\" class=\"referenceInPop\">consecrated</a> for the <a href=\"/topic/gathering\" class=\"referenceInPop\">gethering</a> of the Saints.” <span class=\"title\">The Evening and the Morning Star</span> reported in November 1832 that “since the gathering commenced, which is a little over a year, the number of the disciples which have come from the east, and which have been <a href=\"/topic/baptism\" class=\"referenceInPop\">baptized</a> in this region, is 465[.] Children and those not members, about 345[.] Total 810.” (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-20-july-1831-dc-57\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 20 July 1831 [D&amp;C\n57]\">Revelation, 20 July 1831</a> [D&amp;C 57:1]; “The Gathering,” <span class=\"title\">The Evening and the Morning Star,</span> Nov. 1832, [5].)</p></body></html>", "number": 40, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": "<p id=\"source-note1\"> <span class=\"title\">The Evening and the Morning Star.</span> Independence, MO, June 1832–July 1833; Kirtland, OH, Dec. 1833–Sept. 1834.</p>"}, {"id": "9896968557164312818", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Revelation 14:7.</p></body></html>", "number": 41, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "18004966126904590530", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-circa-7-march-1831-dc-45\" poptitle=\"Revelation, circa 7 March 1831 [D&amp;C\n45]\">Revelation, ca. 7 Mar. 1831</a> [D&amp;C 45:31].</p></body></ht